    "created_at": "2019-05-17T16:55:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-17T16:55:57Z",
    "body": "Great catch. @cdumez, @jeisinger and/or @tzik, can you advise on what your implementations do here?\r\n\r\nI tried to decipher [Chrome's code](https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/v8_initializer.cc?l=242&rcl=161901cdac90ef3440a60efbcf1119be8dbd9809) but it wasn't clear exactly where all the isolates/script states/contexts were coming from.\r\n\r\nIn particular, the important constraint here is we want to mute the error if it comes from a cross-origin script. I suspect speccing this rigorously will be hard, because even for sync exceptions, the spec there is pretty broken. (https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/3149, https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/958) The current spec's use of \"script\" just apes what we do for sync exceptions.\r\n\r\nRelatedly we have the question of what settings object/realm/global to report the error to. Again, as noted in #958, this is not well specced even for sync errors.\r\n\r\nUgh, I'd forgotten what a mess this is. I think the best we could do for now, until someone has time to tackle the general error reporting interoperability mess, is to pick a behavior that seems reasonable, and write some good tests for it, and add an XXX box to the spec.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
