    "updated_at": "2019-05-20T09:15:37Z",
    "body": "But that forces all the specifications to create a Promise only when there is a script running. Do we know that it the case? And if it is, how can we enforce that for the future specs?\r\nI could see some spec wanting to create promise right before calling some JS callback for example.\r\n\r\n(I don't have strong opinion whether to use muted errors from the script which was running when UA created the Promise - if we can guarantee there is always script running, or default to true or false on muted errors )",
